In article <1990Jun27.171935.11661@bdmrrr.bdm.com> jon@bdmrrr.bdm.com (Jon Humphreys) writes:
>Has anyone ever tried to wish for a wizard of yendor corpse? If
>this works, could you then bring him to life with a wand of undead
>turning? How about applying a tinning kit to him? (Pureed Wizard
>of Yendor?)

It'll work.  (Try it in discovery mode to find out.)  Make sure you
capitalize it correctly.  Also, just wishing up a "wizard corpse" gets you a
corpse of a wizard _player_ (the kind of corpse which appears when you play
a wizard and leave behind a ghost level), not the Wizard of Yendor.

>1) Why can't I N)ame my blessed +1 long sword Excalibur?

You have to get the Excalibur bestowed upon you.  (Or you can directly wish
for one.)

>2) How do you create dragon scale mail from a corpse? 

Polymorph the corpse.  The method will be different in 3.1.

>Also, why is grey dragon scale mail better than other armors

Dragon scale mail has a better base armor class; also, grey in particular will
provide magic resistance which you need to fight the Wizard (and liches).

>3) Does Stormbringer have any special properties besides barely ever
>missing an opponent? 

It drains experience levels from monsters when you hit.  (You don't want a
monster to swing one at _you_ doing that!)

>4) Is it legal (possible) to use a wand of wishing to wish for a
>scroll of recharging, and then recharge the wand when it runs out
>of wishes? 

It's possible, but the wand of wishing can only be recharged once.

>5) How can I create holy water from my potions of water? Is unholy
>water benificial for a chaotic character?

To create holy water, drop water on a lawful altar.

Unholy water on a chaotic character heals 2-12 hit points.
Holy water on a chaotic character does 2-12 points of damage, but still
cures lycanthropy.
Holy water on a non-chaotic character cures lycanthropy and sickness (food
poisoning).

The non-drinking uses of holy and unholy water are identical for all
alignments.
